      "id": "https://digitechbytes.com/technology-news-gadgets/a-closer-look-at-metr-s-research-on-ai-development-at-anthropic/",
      "url": "https://digitechbytes.com/technology-news-gadgets/a-closer-look-at-metr-s-research-on-ai-development-at-anthropic/",
      "title": "METR says Anthropic may have crossed AI acceleration warning threshold in July",
      "content_html": "AI safety nonprofit Model Evaluation and Threat Research (METR) says Anthropic may have crossed its own early-warning threshold for AI-driven research acceleration as early as July. METR released its review alongside a finding that model capabilities on selected tasks have improved about 1.9 times faster since October 2025. Anthropic’s policy treats a doubling of progress plausibly driven by automated research as a warning trigger, not proof that a specific danger has arrived.\n\nMETR’s review of Anthropic’s August risk report concluded that the company’s public account understated both the estimated acceleration and the uncertainty around it. Figures in an internal version implied a rate of 1.97, METR said. Anthropic had the right to redact the review and removed most of the evidence METR considered informative, saying disclosure could help competing developers. METR also said Anthropic halted a planned audit of how it allocates computing resources between capability and safety research, choosing to focus first on risk assessment.",
